    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48855" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">transmūtātĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		transmuto. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In gen.,
				<i>a changing</i>, <i><span class="en">Vulg.
				Jacob. 1, 17</span></i>. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In partic., <i>a shifting</i>, <i>transposition</i> of letters (post-Aug.; cf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">transpositio, commutatio),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 1, 5, 39</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">9, 4,
		89</span></i>.</div>
